Why This Is Asked
- Tests mastery of lock-free design, memory ordering, and NUMA-awareness in practical inter-thread communication.

Key Concepts
- Lock-free MPSC rings with per-slot sequencing to prevent ABA
- Cache-line alignment and padding to avoid false sharing
- Correct wrap/threshold handling and epoch-based wraparound
- Memory_order_acquire/release semantics on producers and consumer

Code Example
```c
typedef struct {
  uint64_t seq;         // per-slot sequence counter
  uint8_t  payload[64]; // cache-line aligned payload
} slot_t;

typedef struct {
  slot_t *slots;
  size_t N;               // power-of-two
  _Atomic uint64_t tail;    // producer index
  _Atomic uint64_t head;    // consumer index
} pcq_t;

int pcq_push(pcq_t *q, const void *payload);
int pcq_pop(pcq_t *q, void *out);
```

